<title>SWEDEN: Swedish ratings unaffected by EMU decision-Moody's.</title>
<headline>Swedish ratings unaffected by EMU decision-Moody's.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. credit ratings agency Moody's said on Tuesday that its view of Sweden's international credit ratings was unchanged by Sweden's decision not to join Europe's economic and monetary union (EMU) in 1999.  </p>
<p>&quot;It was the stance that was anticipated,&quot; a Moody's spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;It will not affect Sweden's ratings in the near term or the longterm.&quot;</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said events of the past week must have made Sweden even more comfortable with its decision.</p>
<p>&quot;For them it must have been a very clear cut decision,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
